# The `k === 2`, `k === 3`, `k === 4`, `k === 5` and `k === 7` arms of
# `$show` — a struct, an enum, a list, a tuple and an `Option` — each with the
# empty case beside the populated one, because a renderer written for one
# element is a renderer that prints `[, ]` for none.
#
# A struct with no fields renders `Hollow {}` and a payloadless variant renders
# `.Red`: each is the syntax the value is written in, which is the rule the
# whole table is held to. `middle/derives.rs` generates the same shapes for a
# derived `Show`, so a report and a hand-called `show` cannot disagree.
#
# The library carries the types because a test source may not export, which is
# the same reason `cli/tests/conformance/lib/json/shapes.buri` is a separate
# file from the suite that uses it.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a failing assertion on every composite shape: structs, enums, lists, tuples, and the empty case of each"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/shapes", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "fail.txt"
  stream: OUT
}
